    "description": "What: a side's minefield KNOWLEDGE survives a save + load and a replay seek (Minefields MF-14 / KR-15, CE-4624). 'Field E' is an old Hostile anti-personnel field (x 120-140, y 50-110, a mine every 3 m) that NOBODY knows at start; the scenario carries a saved 'Knowledge' section - written by the real save writer (PlaceKnowledgeSection) - in which Friend has MARKED it and cleared a 5 m LANE along y 80 (its six mines cleared). A Friend 'Squad' (Man Leader + Man 1-3, no commander) marches east from (58-70, 80) to (160, 80), beyond the field. Judge: after the load Friend knows the field in full and holds the lane, Hostile knows nothing (before and at the end); the squad goes THROUGH its lane - no halt for a minefield ahead, no mine goes off, every man inside the lane band (y 77.5-82.5) while inside the field - and reaches (160, 80). The replay half (runner --verify-replay): REPLAY, PLAYBACK and the shuffled SEEKs all same - every recorded component, the knowledge, strikes and lane records included, as live (121 snapshots, 2026-11-19, after backend's CE-5041). Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh mf-knowledge-survives"
